// Rules whose dispatch guards skip calls through two memoized rules (bench/logical_exact_test.go).
// The guards of u skip a call of outer, which calls inner before its first terminal; those of x
// and item skip a call of inner alone. Before the "|", x skips a call of inner at each position
// first, so a skipped call of outer finds an entry of inner that answers it, which ends the calls.
// After it, the first skipped calls at a position are those of u, which store the entry of inner
// and then that of outer. After a "y", z looks ahead at u, whose skipped calls run in a lookahead
// and store entries that the calls outside it do not reuse. The loops discard the values, so that
// the calls in them and in the lookahead call the same rules: the value-free forms of x, u and
// item, and through them of outer and inner.
package chain

@start
rule doc = (-x / -u / -item / z)* ("|" (-u / -item / z)*)? $$
rule x = inner ";" / "e"
rule u = outer "!" / outer "?" / "c"
rule item = inner "." / "b"
rule z = "y" &u
rule outer = inner "-"
rule inner = "a" tail
rule tail = [a-z]*
